        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="3872.18388683715" OwnPage="12" ItemID="196557584" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5303435300678" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Scene"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Kitchen, evening. She's loading the dishwasher, he's sitting in the living room."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;Can you put a load of laundry on?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="He comes into the kitchen, looks at the machine."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;Uh... which setting was it again?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She sighs, steps forward."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;Never mind, I'll do it.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="He goes back to the living room. She stands in front of the machine, face closed."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Later in the evening."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;You could at least make an effort.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;Last time I tried to help, you went back and redid everything. So what's the point.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Silence. Each on their own."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Do You Recognize Yourself?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="I experience this scene: never · sometimes · often"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="In this scene, I'm more like: the one who asks · the one who &quot;doesn't know&quot; · both depending on the moment"/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="4507.4591624277" OwnPage="13" ItemID="196861936" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5300285694373" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Before the Analysis — One Important Thing"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're reading this booklet, it's probably because something isn't working. Because you're tired of carrying more than your share. Because you feel that no matter what you do, it's never good enough. Because the same arguments keep coming back — about the same topics, with the same words — and you no longer really know how to get out of them."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What you feel is real. The exhaustion is real. The frustration is real. This booklet is not going to tell you that you're wrong to feel them."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="But it will offer you something a little uncomfortable: to also look at what's happening on your side. Not to make you feel guilty. Not to say you're just as wrong as the other person. But because it's the only place from which you can truly change something."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="We can't change the other person. We can change what we do — and observe how the system reconfigures."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="That's all this booklet asks of you."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="4507.4591624277" OwnPage="14" ItemID="193571664" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5300285694373" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="193574480" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="What's Really Happening"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The scene you just read, you may have lived dozens of times. The details change — the washing machine, the dishes, the groceries, the bathroom. But the structure stays the same. One asks. The other doesn't know, or pretends not to know. One takes over. The other leaves. And in the evening, something heavy floats in the air without anyone quite knowing what to do with it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What's happening on the surface looks like an organizational problem. Who does what. Who knows what. What's really happening is different."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A system has settled in — gradually, without anyone having decided it. Like all systems, it has its own logic. It sustains itself. And it costs enormously — not in energy spent on the tasks, but in resentment that accumulates, in distance that settles, in the image of the other that slowly distorts."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This isn't an argument about laundry. It's an argument about who is responsible for what in this relationship — and what that says about each person."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What Each Person Is Really Living"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Let's start with her — because if you recognize yourself in this role, you deserve to have what you're really carrying named."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Managing the home largely alone is exhausting. Not just physically. It's the mental load — that permanent list in your head of what still needs to be done, what's going to run out, what you'll need to remember to organize. A list no one else carries. And when you finally ask for help, you get a blank look in front of the washing machine — a machine that's been running in this apartment for years."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What you feel there isn't a bad mood. It's deep exhaustion. And something that looks like loneliness."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Now, him."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you recognize yourself in the other role — the one who &quot;doesn't know,&quot; the one who goes back to the living room — you might know this feeling: whatever you do, it's always redone, corrected, fixed. You load the dishwasher, she reorganizes the glasses. You fold the laundry, she refolds the piles. You try to do the right thing — and the message you receive, without anyone saying it in words, is that it's not enough. That your way of doing things isn't the right way."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="At some point, you stop trying. Not out of laziness. Out of discouragement."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both of these experiences are real. Both are legitimate. And both feed the same system — without either person having wanted it."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="5142.73443801826" OwnPage="15" ItemID="193574480" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5297136088073" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="193571664"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="5142.73443801826" OwnPage="16" ItemID="193577296" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5297136088073" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Game Being Played — Without Anyone Having Decided It"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="In psychology, this is called a game — not in the fun sense, but in the sense of a scenario that repeats itself, with fixed roles, and always the same conclusion. A game where everyone loses, but where everyone keeps playing anyway."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This one is called &quot;The Wooden Leg&quot; — and it looks like this."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There are three roles in this game. The "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the one who suffers, who can't, who is overwhelmed. The "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Rescuer"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the one who takes charge, who fixes, who does it instead. And the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the one who accuses, who criticizes, who judges."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What makes this game insidious is that the roles shift. Watch how it plays out in the scene."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She arrives with a request — &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="can you put a load on?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; But that request isn't neutral. It comes after several times it hasn't been done. It already carries, silently, the expectation of failure. That's the position of the"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH=" Persecutor in waiting "/>
                <ITEXT CH="— not out of malice, but because the history between them has already written the next chapter."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="He senses it. Not consciously. But he senses that whatever he does, it probably won't be good enough. So he enters as the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I don't know how"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; is a way of saying &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I'd rather not try than try and fail."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She takes over. She becomes the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Rescuer"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — she solves, she does it, she keeps the home running. And he goes back to the living room — a relieved "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=", who has avoided the criticism."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Then in the evening, she criticizes. She shifts to "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". And he plays his trump card — &quot;l"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="ast time I tried to help, you went back and redid everything"/>
                <ITEXT CH=".&quot; He's right. And that fact places her, momentarily, as the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" of her own way of doing things."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She's trapped. He's trapped. And tomorrow, the same scene will start again."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="5778.00971360881" OwnPage="17" ItemID="193581136" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5293986481773" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="193592832" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="What Each Person Gets from It — the Hard Part to Read"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This is the most uncomfortable section. The one where you might feel like closing this booklet."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Because this system persists not because one is lazy and the other courageous. It persists because it's useful — not consciously, not deliberately, but really — to both of them."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For her. Carrying everything gives something. It's not just a burden — it's also a position. The position of the one who knows, who acts, who holds things together. A form of control over the space and over how things are done. And sometimes something deeper: the conviction that if she lets go, everything falls apart. That her value in this relationship partly depends on what she does for him."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="It's not her fault. It's often something learned very early — that taking care of others is what makes us loveable."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For him. Not knowing protects something. If I don't do it, I can't do it wrong. If I give up quickly, she takes over — and I avoid being evaluated. This strategy has a history too. Somewhere, at some point, not trying was less painful than trying and being corrected."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Reading this might create resistance. That's normal. It's not an accusation — it's an invitation to look honestly at what this system gives you, right now. Because as long as we don't see what we get from it, we don't really understand why we keep playing."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The &quot;Done Right&quot; Trap — A Word for the One Who Takes Over"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There is something specific worth naming — because it's often invisible to the person who does it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When you've been managing the home for a long time, you develop a way of doing things. An organizational logic that works, that's efficient, that has proven itself. Laundry sorted in a certain way. The dishwasher loaded in a certain order. Groceries listed according to a certain system."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This isn't arbitrary perfectionism. It's accumulated experience."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The problem is that this way of doing things becomes an implicit standard — never really articulated, never really shared. And when the other person tries, in their own way, with their own habits — and the result doesn't match that standard — something triggers. A sigh. A quiet correction. A quick redo — &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="never mind, I'll redo it."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="That gesture — even done with no intention of hurting — sends a very clear message to the other person: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="what you do isn't good enough."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And the other person, who did try, takes note. Next time, they'll try less. Then not at all. And you find yourself complaining that they do nothing — when you, without meaning to, trained them not to."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A question worth asking honestly:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Am I redoing this because it's truly necessary — or because it wasn't done the way I would have done it?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Those two reasons aren't the same thing. The first is a question of outcome — something isn't working, it needs correcting. The second is a question of preference. And preferences can be negotiated."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What if you left the laundry folded differently — but folded? What if you left the kitchen tidied according to his logic — not yours, but a logic nonetheless?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What would that truly change? And what would it free up — for you, for him, for both of you?"/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="5778.00971360881" OwnPage="18" ItemID="193592832" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5293986481773" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="193581136"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="7048.56026478991" OwnPage="21" ItemID="193595648" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5287687269172" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="193598464" BACKITEM="239811744"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="7048.56026478991" OwnPage="22" ItemID="193598464" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5287687269172" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="193595648"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="10860.2119183332" OwnPage="34" ItemID="193561632" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5268789631399" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="201932928" BACKITEM="239806080"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="11495.4871939238" OwnPage="35" ItemID="201932928" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5265640025107" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="193561632"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="11495.4871939238" OwnPage="36" ItemID="201941424" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5265640025107" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="What We Really Need — the NVC Angle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Before going further, one important point."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="In this scene, the two protagonists are not in the same position — and they don't have the same needs. Mixing them means missing something essential."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What follows offers two separate readings. Not to identify a guilty party and a victim. To allow each person to honestly recognize what's activated in them — and find their own exit."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And in both cases, the same rule applies: a need belongs to me. It doesn't depend on what the other person does or doesn't do. I am responsible for finding how to meet it — not for waiting for the other person to guess."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're the one who waited"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What you express through the criticism isn't really anger about the other person's schedule. It's information about what matters to you — and about what erodes when the evenings all look the same."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Read this list. Check what truly resonates."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="12130.7624695144" OwnPage="37" ItemID="201947088" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5262490418816" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Once your need is identified, complete this sentence:"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need __. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is __.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few examples:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need connection. What I choose to do is propose one evening a week that's just for us — not necessarily anything big, just the two of us without screens.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need fun. What I choose to do is suggest something spontaneous this weekend — not over-plan, just suggest.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need intimacy. What I choose to do is clearly say what I'd like — rather than hoping the other person will guess.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're the one who came home"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What you're experiencing when coming home late and tired isn't indifference. It's often exhaustion. And exhaustion has its own needs — that deserve to be named, not silenced."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Read this list. Check what truly resonates."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="12130.7624695144" OwnPage="38" ItemID="201944256" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5262490418816" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Once your need is identified, complete this sentence:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need __. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is __.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few examples:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need space. What I choose to do is say when I get home — one sentence, not an explanation — that I need ten minutes before being there.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need empathy. What I choose to do is ask the other person to hear me for two minutes about my day before we move on to anything else.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need gentleness. What I choose to do is name what I need when I get home — rather than waiting for the atmosphere to give it to me or not.&quot;"/>
                <trail PARENT="narration"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="12766.0377451048" OwnPage="39" ItemID="201935760" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5259340812525" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="201949920" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle LANGUAGE="frp"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Decompression Buffer — A Simple and Underrated Idea"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There is something concrete that many couples have never really established — not because it's complicated, but because nobody talked about it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="It's the buffer."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A short moment — five, ten minutes — between the front door and the shared evening. Not to ignore each other. To come back to yourself before coming back to the other person."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For the one coming home: put things down, breathe, change. Not to disappear — to truly arrive."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For the one who waited: leave this moment free of expectation, free of questions, free of tension. Not out of resignation — by choice. Because the other person who arrives truly is better than the other person who arrives as a facade."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This buffer isn't a luxury. It's a condition for the evening to begin differently than with a collision."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Belief That Complicates Everything — &quot;It Should Be Spontaneous&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There is an implicit conviction in many couples that causes enormous damage without ever being named."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="It looks like this: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="setting a framework, planning moments, making explicit what we need — that means admitting something isn't working anymore. A real couple doesn't need all that. It should come naturally."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This conviction is beautiful. And it's false."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Or rather — it might describe the first months of a relationship, when everything is new and the other person occupies all your attention. But over time, in the fatigue of full weeks, in the routine that settles in — waiting for it to come naturally is waiting for the other person to guess. And nobody truly guesses. Not sustainably."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What creates connection over time is often the opposite of spontaneity: it's decision. Deciding that tonight, we're together. Deciding to say what we'd like. Deciding not to let the week decide for us."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This isn't killing spontaneity. It's creating the conditions for it to exist."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Saying What Matters — a Dance, Not a Schedule"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What's missing in this scene — and in many evenings like it — is a simple agreement on what matters to each person."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not a list of rules. Not a planning chart. A conversation."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Tonight I felt like doing this. Is it possible — or is it tomorrow?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="That sentence changes everything. It says what you'd like without demanding it. It leaves the other person free to respond. It opens a negotiation that isn't a conflict — it's a way of finding each other."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And when both know what matte"/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="12766.0377451048" OwnPage="40" ItemID="201949920" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5259340812525" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="201935760"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="13401.3130206954" OwnPage="41" ItemID="201938592" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5256191206234" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="201955584" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Alert Not to Miss"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The exit from this game isn't to come home earlier — or to criticize less."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Coming home earlier without changing the dynamic produces the same scene in a different context. And holding back the criticism without addressing the real need creates a pressure that ends up exploding elsewhere."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What changes something is the shift: from &quot;what do I want the other person to do&quot; to &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="what do I need to nourish tonight — and how do I nourish it"/>
                <ITEXT CH="?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Exits"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 1 — Notice your role in the moment"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The next time this scene is triggered — or when you sense it approaching — one internal question:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Right now, am I more in the mode of waiting, accusing, or defending?"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Just name it. Not analyze. Naming creates a space between reflex and reaction."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="waiting"/>
                <ITEXT CH=": what exactly are you waiting for — and can you ask for it directly rather than hoping?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="accusing"/>
                <ITEXT CH=": what's really activated — tonight's frustration, or something that's been building for longer?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="defending"/>
                <ITEXT CH=": what did you need to find when you got home — and can you say it?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 2 — Say what you need before the evening begins (solo)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This exercise requires a little anticipation."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Before the other person comes home — or before coming home yourself — one internal question:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Tonight, what do "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" truly need?"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not a list. One thing. The most honest one."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Then try to express it simply, without criticism, before the tension builds. A few example formulations to adapt:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Tonight I need us to be truly together — not on our phones. Can we do that?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I had a hard day. I need 10 minutes to breathe before I'm truly available.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I needed to know what time you'd be home. Next time, could you send a message?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="These sentences don't fix everything. But they say something true — and they leave the other person the possibility of responding rather than defending."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 3 — Reconnect to your need in the moment (solo)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When tension builds, when the criticism arrives or when the urge to withdraw is strong — pause. Ten seconds."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Complete mentally:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;The need that's activated in me right now is __. And something I can do to meet it tonight is __.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not to erase the frustration. To choose what to do with it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 4 — The calm conversation (together)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="To have outside the moment of tension — not the night of the late return, not during the silent dinner. The next day, calmly, 20 minutes."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Each person completes these sentences separately, in writing:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;When this scene happens, what's activated in me is...&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;The real need behind my reaction is...&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;What I would need from the other person in these moments — not that they change, but...&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Then you share — each person reads, the other listens without interrupting. The goal is not to convince each other. It's to hear what the other person is truly experiencing beneath the surface."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Then, one question to explore together:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;What could we do — a concrete, simple, realistic gesture — so that these evenings go differently?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not a solemn commitment. An experiment. That can be adjusted, revisited, abandoned if it doesn't work."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="13401.3130206954" OwnPage="42" ItemID="201955584" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5256191206234" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="201961248" BACKITEM="201938592"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="14036.588296286" OwnPage="43" ItemID="201961248" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5253041599943" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="201955584"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="14036.588296286" OwnPage="44" ItemID="201958416" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5253041599943" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle FONTSIZE="14"/>
                <ITEXT FONTSIZE="11" CH="Feeding Your Free Child — Reminder"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONTSIZE="9.5" CH="As in the previous scene — and in all the ones that follow — there is something playing in the background of this dynamic."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONTSIZE="9.5" CH="When we're exhausted, when we're waiting for the other person to fill something, when we come home on our knees with no resource to be present — it's often a sign that we've forgotten ourselves somewhere in the day."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONTSIZE="9.5" CH="The Free Child is that part of you that has its own desires, that nourishes itself on simple things — a moment alone, an activity that restores you, something that exists just for you. When it's nourished, the waiting for the other person diminishes naturally. You arrive less empty, less demanding, less on the edge."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONTSIZE="9.5" CH="The question to ask yourself tonight:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONTSIZE="9.5" CH="What did I do today — even five minutes — just for myself?"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONTSIZE="9.5" CH="Tracking — 7 Days"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONTSIZE="9.5" CH="Every evening, two minutes."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="14671.8635718765" OwnPage="45" ItemID="201964080" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5249891993652" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="One question per evening — just the one for that day:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Monday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Tonight, which role did I spend the most time in — "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH=", "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH=", or "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Rescuer"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Tuesday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What did I want to say — and didn't?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Wednesday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What need was activated tonight — and how did I choose to meet it?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Thursday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What would have happened if I'd said what I needed, directly?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Friday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="How did I nourish my Free Child today — and what did it change in my availability for the other person?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Saturday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What belief about the other person did this week come to confirm — and is it really true?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Sunday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="If I replaced the criticism with the real need — what sentence would that give me?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The next scene has no open criticism. Just a phone call that didn't go well — and two very different ways of being there for someone who's hurting."/>
                <trail PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="1"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="14671.8635718765" OwnPage="46" ItemID="201952752" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5249891993652" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Scene 3 — The Call With Her Mother"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Fix Me&quot;"/>
                <trail PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
            </StoryText>
            <PageItemAttributes>
                <ItemAttribute Name="tdm" Type="string" Value="Scène 3 — L'appel avec la mère" Parameter="" Relationship="none" RelationshipTo="" AutoAddTo="none"/>
            </PageItemAttributes>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="15307.1388474671" OwnPage="47" ItemID="201978240" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5246742387361" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="15307.1388474671" OwnPage="48" ItemID="201969744" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5246742387361" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Scene"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Living room, evening. She hangs up, puts her phone on the table. Her face says the call didn't go well."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;My mother, unbelievable. She made another comment about how I'm raising the kids. In front of them too.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;What did you say to her?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;Nothing. I didn't want it to escalate.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;Next time, you could calmly tell her it's not her place. You don't have to put up with that.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;I know. But it's not that simple with her.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;I understand, but if you don't set a boundary now, it's going to keep happening.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Silence. She looks away."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;Just forget it.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She gets up, goes to the kitchen. He stays on the couch, perplexed — he tried to help."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Do You Recognize Yourself?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="I experience this scene: never · sometimes · often"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="In this scene, I'm more like: the one who hung up · the one who advises · both depending on the moment"/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="15942.4141230576" OwnPage="49" ItemID="201966912" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.524359278107" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="201981072" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Before the Analysis — One Important Thing"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you recognize yourself in this scene, you probably know both sides."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="You know what it's like to hang up with something heavy in your chest — and to just want someone to be there. Not to explain. Not to structure. Just to stay, and say with their eyes or their words: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I see that this is hard, and you're not alone with it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And you might know the other side too: seeing someone you love suffer, and not knowing what to do with your hands. The discomfort of helplessness. The sincere desire to help — which arrives in the form of solutions, because it's the only tool at hand."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both are legitimate. Both are human."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What this booklet will offer you is a look at what's really happening in the space between these two needs — when one is seeking to be heard, and the other is seeking to be useful. Not to identify a guilty party. To see the mechanics — and find how to get out together."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What's Really Happening"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="On the surface, it's a conversation about her mother. What's really happening has nothing to do with what should or shouldn't be said next time."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She's just been through something painful. A comment from her mother — not the first, probably not the last — that touches a precise spot: the way she raises her children, meaning something essential to who she is. She hangs up carrying this pain. She talks about it. Not to find a solution — to not be alone with it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What she's looking for when she puts her phone down and says &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="my mother, unbelievable"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; isn't an action plan. It's someone who says: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I see that you're hurting. It makes sense to hurt. I'm here."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="He hears something different. He hears a problem — and problems get solved. He activates. He suggests. He structures. He does what he does best when someone he loves is suffering: he looks for how to fix it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The problem is that what she's bringing him isn't broken. It's painful. And pain doesn't get fixed — it gets traversed, accompanied."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When he says &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="you could calmly tell her it's not her place"/>
                <ITEXT CH=",&quot; he's convinced he's helping. She hears: you didn't handle that well. When he says &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="if you don't set a boundary now, it's going to keep happening,"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; he thinks he's right — he probably is. She hears: you're responsible for what your mother does to you."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She says &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="just forget it"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; and leaves the room. He stays perplexed, sincerely. He tried."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="That's the game. Nobody is wrong. Nobody wins."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="15942.4141230576" OwnPage="50" ItemID="201981072" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.524359278107" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="201966912"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="16577.6893986481" OwnPage="51" ItemID="201983904" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.524044317476" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="201972576" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Game Being Played — Without Anyone Having Decided It"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="In psychology, this type of scene has a precise name: the &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Yes But"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; game. It's one of the most common patterns in couples — and one of the most misunderstood, precisely because it looks like a request for help."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The structure is always the same. Someone presents a problem. The other suggests a solution. The first responds: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Yes, but..."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; — and explains why it can't work. The other suggests something else. &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Yes, but..."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; The sequence repeats until exhaustion — and ends with a silence, a sigh, or a &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="just forget it"/>
                <ITEXT CH=".&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What confuses the one who suggests is the conviction of having correctly heard a request for help. They're right about the form. They're wrong about the substance."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The apparent request is: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="help me find a solution."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; The real request — the one operating beneath the surface — sounds more like: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="confirm to me that the situation is truly hard, and that I'm not alone with what I'm feeling."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The solutions proposed can't be accepted — not because they're bad, but because they would answer the wrong question. Accepting a solution would close something that isn't ready to be closed. It's not bad faith. It's mechanical."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Victim Who Awakens the Rescuer"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There's something important to see here — before the words even arrive."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When she hangs up with that face, when she says &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="my mother, unbelievable"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; — something activates in him automatically. Not a decision. A reflex. The other person's suffering — even involuntary, even legitimate — awakens the Rescuer. And the Rescuer arrives with solutions, because that's his way of loving."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This reflex isn't a flaw. It's often what makes him attentive, present, reliable. But it has a blind spot: it responds to visible distress without verifying what the other person truly needs. It assumes that suffering calls for help — and that helping means suggesting."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The more she expresses her pain, the more his Rescuer activates. The more his Rescuer activates, the more she feels misunderstood. The more she feels misunderstood, the more the pain closes off — or explodes. And the loop turns."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Rescuer believes he's serving the other person. He's first serving his own need not to feel helpless in the face of the suffering of someone he loves. It's not a reproach — it's a mechanism. And seeing it is already beginning to step out of it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Karpman Drama Triangle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There are three roles in this game. The "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the one who suffers, who shares, who seeks to be heard. The "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Rescuer"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the one who suggests, who structures, who wants to fix. And the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the one who, without meaning to, ends up hurting or being hurt."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She arrives as "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — in the technical sense: she's enduring something she didn't choose, and she's talking about it. He immediately enters as "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Rescuer"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — it's his natural movement in the face of the other's suffering."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The twist comes when his solutions are rejected. He shifts to "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — he tried, he's not understood, what's the point. And she, who was just trying to be heard, finds herself having to manage his perplexity — on top of the pain from the call. She becomes, despite herself, the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" of someone who wanted to help."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" who shares → awakens → "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Rescuer"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" who suggests → rejection → "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Rescuer"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" becomes "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" → the one who was suffering becomes "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" → silence"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both leave the scene with something unpleasant. Her: alone with her pain, and also guilty for having hurt him. Him: misunderstood in his efforts, with the diffuse feeling of having missed something without knowing what."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What Each Person Gets from It — the Hard Part"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This system persists because it confirms something for each person — and because it protects each person from something."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For her: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="when I talk to him about what truly hurts me, I end up managing his reaction."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; This conviction makes future confidences less likely — she'll learn not to talk about it, to handle things alone, to only show what won't trigger advice. Distance settles quietly, without anyone having decided it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There's something deeper too. As long as the problem with her mother is unsolvable — as long as no solution works — she doesn't have to change anything in that relationship. She doesn't have to set a boundary that frightens her. She doesn't have to face the fact that this relationship is perhaps structurally painful. The game allows her to stay in the suffering — which is real — without having to confront what it asks of her. It's uncomfortable, but it's known."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For him: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="when she suffers, I don't know what to do."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; This helplessness is uncomfortable — and the reflex to suggest solutions is precisely a way of not staying in that discomfort. If I have a plan, I'm not helpless. The problem is that the plan misses the need. And missing the need confirms the helplessness — and therefore reinforces the reflex next time."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Every rejected solution confirms for him that he's trying — that he's present, that he's making efforts. The game allows him to avoid the discomfort of simply being there, doing nothing, not being useful. That helplessness is harder to hold than the accumulation of solutions that don't work."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both are trapped in something they built together, without seeing it."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="16577.6893986481" OwnPage="52" ItemID="201972576" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.524044317476" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="201975408" BACKITEM="201983904"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="17212.9646742387" OwnPage="53" ItemID="201975408" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5237293568451" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="201972576"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="17212.9646742387" OwnPage="54" ItemID="201995232" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5237293568451" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="What We Really Need — the NVC Angle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Here too, the two protagonists are not in the same position — and they don't have the same needs. Two separate readings, therefore."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And in both cases, the same rule: a need belongs to me. It doesn't depend on what the other person does or doesn't do. I am responsible for finding how to meet it — not for waiting for the other person to guess."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're the one who hung up"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What you express through the &quot;just forget it&quot; isn't rejection. It's information about what you needed — and what you didn't find."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Read this list. Check what truly resonates."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="17848.2399498293" OwnPage="55" ItemID="201989568" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5234143962142" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="201992400" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Once your need is identified, complete this sentence:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need __. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is __.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few examples:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need presence. What I choose to do is say it before starting — 'I need to talk to you about something, but right now I mostly need you to listen, no advice for now.'&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need validation. What I choose to do is ask explicitly for what I'd like: 'just tell me it was hard.'&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need safety. What I choose to do is name what closes me off — 'when advice comes quickly, I feel less safe continuing to talk.'&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're the one who suggested solutions"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What you were doing by suggesting wasn't indifference to her pain. It was, in your way, a form of love. But what you were looking for, you, in that exchange, also deserves to be looked at."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Read this list. Check what truly resonates."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Once your need is identified, complete this sentence:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need __. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is __.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few examples:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need clarity. What I choose to do is ask before suggesting: 'do you want us to figure out what to do, or do you mostly need me to listen?'&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need connection. What I choose to do is stay there without speaking — just be present, and let that be enough.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need usefulness. What I choose to do is remind myself that truly listening is also a form of help — maybe the most useful one here.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Sentence That Changes Everything"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There is one short sentence — a question — that can defuse this scene before it starts. It requires no theoretical work. It just needs to be asked."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Do you want us to figure out what to do, or do you mostly need me to listen?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This question does several things at once. It tells the other person: I heard that something is difficult. It leaves them the choice — no presupposition about what they need. And it saves the listener from navigating blind, from suggesting solutions that will miss, from ending up perplexed on the couch."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="It's not magic. But it short-circuits the game before it starts."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="17848.2399498293" OwnPage="56" ItemID="201992400" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5234143962142" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="201989568"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="18483.5152254199" OwnPage="57" ItemID="201986736" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5230994355832" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225640560" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Alert Not to Miss"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The exit from this game isn't to stop suggesting solutions — or to force yourself to stay silent."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Restraining yourself in silence is another form of the same discomfort. She'll sense it. And constrained silence isn't presence — it's absence with a clear conscience."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The real question for him isn't &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="how do I help her handle her mother?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; It's &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="what's happening in me when she's suffering and I can't do anything?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; And more precisely: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="are my solutions truly serving her need — or are they first serving my need not to feel helpless?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The real question for her isn't &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="how do I make him understand that he's not listening to me?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; It's &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="what's stopping me from directly saying what I need — not a solution, just to be heard?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Exits"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 1 — Ask before responding (solo — the listener)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The next time the other person shares something difficult, before suggesting anything — one question:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Do you want us to figure out what to do, or do you mostly need me to listen?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Just that. No interpretation, no assumption. The answer says everything needed to know how to be useful in that moment."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If the answer is &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I need you to listen"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; — stay. Suggest nothing. Let the silence do its work. And if the discomfort of helplessness rises, note it internally without responding to it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 2 — Say what you need before starting (solo — the one speaking)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Before beginning a difficult conversation, a short sentence saying what you need — without waiting for the other person to guess:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need to talk to you about something, but right now I mostly need you to listen — no advice for now.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Or, even shorter: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I just need you to be there."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This sentence might seem unnecessary — why should I have to ask to be listened to? But it short-circuits the loop before it starts. And it gives the other person what they also need: knowing how to be present."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 3 — Reflect before responding (solo — the listener)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When the other person shares something painful, the solution reflex comes quickly — before you've even truly heard."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A simple practice: before responding, let a silence pass. Not an awkward silence — a silence that says I'm taking time to truly receive what you just said. Then, instead of suggesting, reflect. Name what you heard beneath the words."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;That sounds like it was really hard.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;A comment like that, in front of the kids too — that's hurtful.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;You didn't need that tonight.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I understand that you didn't want it to escalate.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="These sentences solve nothing. They do something more useful: they tell the other person that they're not alone with what they feel. And often, that's all they needed."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 4 — Name the game together (together)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A conversation to have outside the moment of tension — not the night of the call, not in the still-fresh discomfort. A few days later, calmly, 20 minutes."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Each person completes these sentences separately, in writing:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;When I share something painful, what I need first is...&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;When the other person suffers and I can't do anything, what happens in me is...&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;What I find hard to say in these moments is...&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Then you share — each person reads, the other listens without interrupting, without defending. The goal isn't to convince each other. It's to hear what the other person is truly experiencing beneath the surface."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Then, one question to explore together:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Can we give ourselves a signal — a word, a short phrase — that says 'right now I need to be heard, not advised'? Something we both recognize, and that avoids having to explain this in the moment of pain.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not a secret code. A shortcut. That can be tested, adjusted, abandoned if it doesn't work."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="18483.5152254199" OwnPage="58" ItemID="225640560" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5230994355832" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225654720" BACKITEM="201986736"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="19118.7905010104" OwnPage="59" ItemID="225654720" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5227844749523" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="225640560"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="19118.7905010104" OwnPage="60" ItemID="225643392" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5227844749523" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Feeding Your Free Child — Reminder"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There is something operating in the background of this scene — and in all the ones that follow."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When he can't stay in discomfort without acting, it's often a sign that something isn't nourished elsewhere. That the only way he knows to be useful — and therefore to have value — goes through solutions, plans, actions. And when that doesn't work, he's left empty."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When she can't directly say what she needs — when she prefers to close off rather than ask — it's often a sign that something older is activated. Something telling her that her needs are too much, or that they won't be heard anyway."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Free Child is that part of you that plays, that feels, that expresses itself without calculation. The part that existed before you learned to be useful, or not to ask for too much. It hasn't disappeared. It's just waiting for a little space."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The question to ask yourself tonight:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What did I do today — even five minutes — just for myself? Not to be useful. Not to manage. Just for myself."/>
                <trail PARENT="narration"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="19754.0657766009" OwnPage="61" ItemID="225657552" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5224695143214" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Free Child Tracker — 7 days"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY" ALIGN="3"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Every evening, one minute."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="3"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The end-of-week question:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY" ALIGN="3"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY" ALIGN="3"/>
                <ITEXT CH="On the days when I nourished my Free Child — did I have more or less urge to solve, to control, to close off? Is there a connection?"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY" ALIGN="3"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Tracking — 7 Days"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY" ALIGN="3"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Every evening, two minutes."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY" ALIGN="3"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="19754.0657766009" OwnPage="62" ItemID="225649056" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5224695143214" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="One question per evening — just the one for that day:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Monday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Tonight, which role did I spend the most time in — "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH=", "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Rescuer"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH=", or "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Tuesday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="When I felt like suggesting a solution — what was I trying to do with my own discomfort?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Wednesday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="When I shared something difficult, did I say what I needed — or did I let the other person guess?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Thursday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What's stopping me from directly saying &quot;I need to be heard, not advised&quot;?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Friday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="How did I nourish my Free Child today — and what did it change in my availability for the other person?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Saturday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What belief about the other person did this week come to confirm — and is it really true?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Sunday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="If I replaced the &quot;just forget it&quot; with what I truly needed — what sentence would that give me?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The next scene takes place in a kitchen, on an ordinary evening. There's a phone, a bank statement, and a bag left on the table. And a question nobody has yet clearly asked."/>
                <trail PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="1"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="20389.3410521915" OwnPage="63" ItemID="225651888" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5221545536904" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="20389.3410521915" OwnPage="64" ItemID="225646224" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5221545536904" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Scene 4 — Finances"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;The Grand Ledger&quot;"/>
                <trail PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
            </StoryText>
            <PageItemAttributes>
                <ItemAttribute Name="tdm" Type="string" Value="Scène 4 — Les finances" Parameter="" Relationship="none" RelationshipTo="" AutoAddTo="none"/>
            </PageItemAttributes>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="21024.616327782" OwnPage="65" ItemID="225660384" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5218395930595" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="21024.616327782" OwnPage="66" ItemID="225668880" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5218395930595" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Scene"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Kitchen, a weekday evening. He's checking the bank account on his phone. She comes in with a bag."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;Did you go shopping again?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;I needed a few things.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;We said we'd be careful this month. We're already in the red.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;It wasn't much. And besides, it's my money too.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;I'm not saying it's not your money. I'm saying we have a shared budget and you're not taking it into account.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;Are you monitoring everything I do now?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="He puts down his phone. Silence."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;Just forget it.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She puts down the bag, leaves the room. The bag stays on the table."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Do You Recognize Yourself?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="I experience this scene: never · sometimes · often"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="In this scene, I'm more like: the one who monitors · the one who spends · both depending on the moment"/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="21659.8916033726" OwnPage="67" ItemID="225671712" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5215246324286" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225674544" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Before the Analysis — One Important Thing"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you recognize yourself in this scene, you probably know both sides."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="You know what it's like to look at a statement and feel something tighten. Not malice — a real, diffuse anxiety, hard to articulate without it coming out as a criticism. The feeling that the framework you'd set isn't holding. That decisions aren't really being made together. And not knowing how to say it without seeming like you're monitoring."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And you might know the other side too: coming home with something — a purchase, a gesture for yourself — and sensing the gaze before you've even put the bag down. The feeling of having to justify yourself for something that didn't seem so serious. And the question rising, not always articulated: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="am I free in this relationship"/>
                <ITEXT CH="?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both are real. Both are legitimate. And they rarely meet — because each is responding to what they hear, not to what the other is really saying."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What this booklet will offer you is a look at what's really happening beneath the surface — not to identify who's wrong, but because it's the only place from which something can change."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What's Really Happening"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="On the surface, it's an argument about an overspent budget. What's really happening has almost nothing to do with the amount on the statement."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Money in a couple is never just money. It's the terrain on which much more loaded questions play out: who decides, who controls, who trusts, who is free, who is responsible. What each person does with money — spending, holding back, monitoring, ignoring — says something about what they need and what they fear. Not consciously. But really."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There's also, often, a question the two of them have never truly settled — not because they've avoided it, but because it's never been clearly posed."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="How much is money "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="ours"/>
                <ITEXT CH="?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The shift from "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="my"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" money to "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="our"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" money is not automatic. It requires a decision — conscious, explicit, chosen together — about what goes into the common pool, what stays separate, and what that says about how you bind yourselves. Some couples merge everything from the start, without discussing it. Others maintain separate zones, without having truly decided that either. And many live in a fuzzy in-between — a shared account for expenses, personal accounts for the rest — without ever having named what that organization says about their relationship."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="It's my money too"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; — that sentence in the scene isn't just a claim to autonomy. It's a sign that this question hasn't yet been resolved. Not between the numbers. Between them."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And as long as it hasn't been, the budget argument goes in circles — because it's looking for a financial answer to a question that is first relational."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Here, he opens the account and sees an overspend. What he feels isn't just financial anxiety — it's something more diffuse: the sense that decisions aren't being made together, that the agreement isn't being respected, that the shared framework isn't holding. It's not yet a criticism — it's an anxiety looking for an outlet. And it comes out through monitoring."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She comes home with a bag. She doesn't feel she's done something serious — or if she does, she doesn't want to admit it. When he points out the overspend, she hears something other than what he's saying. She hears: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="you're not reliable. I have to monitor you. You're not free"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". And to that sentence, she responds — not to the budget."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Are you monitoring everything I do"/>
                <ITEXT CH="?&quot; isn't a question about bank statements. It's a question about trust, autonomy, the place she has in this relationship."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Nobody is talking about what they're really talking about. And that's why it doesn't get resolved."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="21659.8916033726" OwnPage="68" ItemID="225674544" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5215246324286" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="225671712"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="22295.1668789632" OwnPage="69" ItemID="225663216" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5212096717976" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225677376" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Ego States Present:"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What's striking: the two are operating from states that cannot meet. His Normative Parent is addressing an Adult that isn't there. Her Rebellious Child is responding to a Parent she doesn't want to acknowledge. The Adult — the one who could talk about budget, needs, shared decisions — is absent on both sides."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Victim Who Awakens the Controller"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There's a reflex here that mirrors what we saw in the previous scene — but reversed."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When he perceives a budget overrun, something activates in him automatically. Not a decision. A protection reflex. The perceived threat — financial, but also relational — awakens the Normative Parent in control mode. He checks, he reframes, he restates the rules."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This reflex isn't arbitrary. It often comes from a precise place: fear of instability, a relationship with money built early, a conviction that if nobody watches everything falls apart. It's not him monitoring "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="her"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — it's him monitoring the system, because the system represents something vital."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="But she doesn't see the system. She sees the gaze on her. And that gaze activates her Rebellious Child — the one who refuses the guardianship, who reclaims her place, who says "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I'm not a child being monitored."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both are reacting to something real. And neither is reacting to what the other is truly saying."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Karpman Drama Triangle — the Drama in Three Acts"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What makes this triangle particular is that it starts before the words even arrive. The game is already underway when she pushes the door open."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Act 1 — before she comes home"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". He checks the account. He sees the overspend. Something tightens. He hasn't said anything yet — but he's already in "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" mode: alone with an anxiety he carries, a framework he monitors, a decision that was made without him. The other person isn't there yet, and the game has already started."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Act 2 — she comes home"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". She puts down the bag. He says: &quot;did you go shopping again?&quot; He shifts to "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — not by intention, but by effect. The question isn't neutral. It points. It evaluates. It places the other in a position of having to justify themselves."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She enters as "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — surprised, or perhaps not entirely. She knew. And something in her had prepared for this."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Act 3 — the twist. &quot;Are you monitoring everything I do?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; She shifts to "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". It's no longer a response to the budget — it's a counter-attack on the terrain of control and freedom. He becomes "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" again: he was just trying to hold to an agreement, and he finds himself accused of monitoring."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Just forget it"/>
                <ITEXT CH=".&quot; He withdraws. The game stops — without a winner, without resolution. The bag stays on the table. And each leaves with the confirmation of what they feared."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" alone with the statement → "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" on her arrival → her as "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" → she shifts to "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" → him as "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" → withdrawal → mutual confirmation of what they already feared"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Hidden Benefit of the Drama"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This triangle persists because it protects something — in each person, differently."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For him: monitoring is a way of not being overwhelmed by an anxiety he doesn't always know how to name. If I have the framework in hand, I'm not helpless. It's not control for control's sake — it's a response to something older, often, around instability or loss. The problem is that this response costs the other person what she needs most: feeling free."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For her: spending without saying anything preserves a zone that belongs to her. A decision made alone, for herself, without negotiation. It's not irresponsibility — it's often a need for autonomy that hasn't yet found another path. The problem is that this path costs the other person what he needs most: feeling like they're on the same team."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both protect something legitimate. And both do so in a way that hurts exactly where the other person is most vulnerable. It's not malice — it's what happens when two real needs have never been spoken aloud."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="22295.1668789632" OwnPage="70" ItemID="225677376" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5212096717976" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225666048" BACKITEM="225663216"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="22930.4421545536" OwnPage="71" ItemID="225666048" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5208947111667" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="225677376"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="22930.4421545536" OwnPage="72" ItemID="225688704" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5208947111667" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225691536" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Why She Spends — Lines of Inquiry"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Before talking about budget, there's a more useful question than &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="how much did you spend?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What was this spending trying to do?"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not to excuse. Not to normalize. But because understanding what's really happening beneath the spending completely changes the nature of the conversation — and opens the possibility of a real response instead of a numbers conflict."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few lines of inquiry — several can coexist, and none is universal:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Spending as self-care"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". After a hard week, a purchase — even small — can be the only way to give yourself something. Not luxury: gentleness. A concrete gesture that says I matter too. If the rest of life is organized around other people's needs, this spending might be the only zone where she chooses for herself."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Spending as a territory of autonomy"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". In a relationship where financial decisions are asymmetric — one who earns more, one who monitors more, one who decides more — spending without asking can be a silent way of reclaiming a place. I'm not asking your permission. It's not rational. It's identity-based."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Spending as emotional regulation"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". Shopping, like other compulsive behaviors, can be a response to a difficult inner state — anxiety, boredom, sadness, a feeling of emptiness. The purchase produces a quick stimulation, a mini-satisfaction. The problem isn't the spending — it's what it comes to cover, which remains whole afterward."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Spending as a test"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". Sometimes, unconsciously, exceeding an agreement is a way of testing the other person's reaction. Will he notice? Will he react? Is he paying attention to what's happening for me? It's not a strategy — it's a need for connection expressing itself the wrong way."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="These lines of inquiry aren't excuses. They're entry points toward a different conversation. The one that begins with &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="what's been going on for you this month?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; rather than &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="you went shopping again."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And for him too, a symmetrical question deserves to be asked: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="why is controlling money so important to me?"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" What does the budget overrun really activate — financial anxiety, or something older around instability, trust, the feeling of being overwhelmed?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There's often something paradoxical in this position. What irritates about the other — the lightness, the impulse, the ability to spend without thinking — is sometimes exactly what one would need oneself. But an overly present inner Parent makes it inaccessible. "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I have to be reasonable. I have to hold things together. This isn't the time"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". And seeing the other grant themselves what you deny yourself creates an irritation that resembles anger — but often hides something softer: sadness, or fear."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What each person does with money also says something deeper — about what they value, what they consider legitimate, what they allow themselves. Two people can have identical incomes and radically different relationships to money — because those relationships aren't built on numbers. They're built on stories. What you saw in your family of origin. What you learned to associate with spending — pleasure, guilt, freedom, danger. What money represented when you were a child — security, scarcity, power, lightness."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This isn't incompatibility. It's a difference in values that hasn't yet been named. And an unnamed difference always ends up expressing itself — as criticism, resistance, or silence."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="23565.7174301442" OwnPage="73" ItemID="225691536" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5205797505358" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="225688704"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="23565.7174301442" OwnPage="74" ItemID="225680208" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5205797505358" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225694368" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle LANGUAGE="fur"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="The Alert Not to Miss"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="The exit from this game isn't to better stick to the budget — or to monitor less."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="Sticking to the budget without changing the dynamic produces an underground tension that explodes elsewhere. And monitoring less without addressing the real anxiety creates an anxiety that looks for another outlet."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="The real question for him isn't &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" LANGUAGE="fur" CH="how do I get her to respect the budget?"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="&quot; It's &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" LANGUAGE="fur" CH="what does the overrun really activate in me — and where does that come from?"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="The real question for her isn't &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" LANGUAGE="fur" CH="how do I make him understand it's my money too?"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="&quot; It's &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" LANGUAGE="fur" CH="what am I looking for when I spend without saying anything — and could that thing be asked for differently?"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="What We Really Need — the NVC Angle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="Before going further, one important point."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="In this scene, the two protagonists are not in the same position — and they don't have the same needs. Mixing them means missing something essential."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="What follows offers two separate readings. Not to identify a guilty party and a victim. To allow each person to honestly recognize what's activated in them — and find their own exit."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="And in both cases, the same rule applies: a need belongs to me. It doesn't depend on what the other person does or doesn't do. I am responsible for finding how to meet it — not for waiting for the other person to guess."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="If you're the one wh"/>
                <ITEXT CPARENT="Default Character Style" CH="o"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH=" monitors"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="What you express through the statement isn't really control. It's information about what's missing — and about what you don't allow yourself."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="There's often something paradoxical in this position. What irritates about the other — the lightness, the impulse, the ability to spend without thinking — is sometimes exactly what you would need yourself. But an overly present inner Parent makes it inaccessible. "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" LANGUAGE="fur" CH="I have to be reasonable. I have to hold things together. This isn't the time"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH=". And seeing the other grant themselves what you deny yourself creates an irritation that resembles anger — but often hides something softer: sadness, or fear."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="The fear, often, of collapse. Of not being able to manage. Someone in survival mode can't project forward — lightness becomes a luxury that seems dangerous. And from that place, monitoring is a clumsy way of trying to build something — a shared framework, a common momentum, a "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" LANGUAGE="fur" CH="we're in this together."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT LANGUAGE="fur" CH="Read this list. Check what truly resonates."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Once your need is identified, complete this sentence:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need __. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is __.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few examples:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need lightness. What I choose to do is allow myself something this week — even small — without justifying it. And observe what that changes in my availability for the other person.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need sharing. What I choose to do is propose a conversation about what we want to build together — not about what went wrong.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need clarity. What I choose to do is name my anxiety directly — not as a criticism, but as something that belongs to me and that I'd like to face together.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're the one who spends"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What you express through the purchase isn't irresponsibility. It's information about what you need — and about what's missing when every decision becomes negotiating territory."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The spending says something that words don't say yet. Sometimes it's self-care — the only gesture this week that was for you. Sometimes it's claimed autonomy — a decision made alone, without having to ask permission. Sometimes it's regulation — something difficult to get through, and the purchase that brings a quick mini-satisfaction. And sometimes, without deciding it, it's a way of testing: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="is he paying attention to what's happening for me?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="It's not a strategy. It's a need that hasn't yet found its direct path."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Read this list. Check what truly resonates."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Once your need is identified, complete this sentence:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need __. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is __.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few examples:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need freedom. What I choose to do is propose that we think together about a personal allowance — money each of us has freely, without justification.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need self-care. What I choose to do is find other ways to do myself good that don't go only through spending — and name what I need rather than looking for it alone.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need vitality. What I choose to do is propose something light this week — nothing big, just something that steps outside the management.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="These two lists don't oppose each other. They never meet in the scene — because the scene doesn't give them space. But they speak, at bottom, of the same thing: two people trying to live, each in their own way, in a space that's meant to be shared."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="24200.9927057348" OwnPage="75" ItemID="225694368" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5202647899049" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225683040" BACKITEM="225680208"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="24200.9927057348" OwnPage="76" ItemID="225683040" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5202647899049" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225697200" BACKITEM="225694368"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="24836.2679813253" OwnPage="77" ItemID="225697200" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5199498292739" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="225683040"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="24836.2679813253" OwnPage="78" ItemID="225685872" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5199498292739" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Feeding Your Free Child"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There is something operating in the background of this scene — and worth naming."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The one who monitors has often locked away their own lightness for a long time. The "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Normative Parent"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" has taken too much space — "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I have to hold things together, I have to manage, this isn't the time"/>
                <ITEXT CH=". And the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Free Child"/>
                <ITEXT CH=", that part that plays, that treats itself, that sometimes spends for no valid reason, has learned to be quiet. The result: reduced emotional availability, underlying irritability, and a quiet jealousy toward the one who seems able to do what you forbid yourself."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The one who spends is trying to nourish their "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Free Child"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — but through a path that triggers conflict rather than creating space. Spending is an attempt at lightness. Not always the most direct one."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both need the same thing — to allow themselves lightness, each in their own way, without it going through money or through the other person."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The question to ask yourself tonight:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What did I do today — even five minutes — just for myself? Not to manage. Not to be responsible. Just for the pleasure of existing."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And an additional question, specific to this scene:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What do I forbid myself — and why? Does this prohibition truly protect me, or does it impoverish me?"/>
                <trail PARENT="narration"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="25471.5432569159" OwnPage="79" ItemID="225700032" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.519634868643" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="225702864" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Exits"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Level 1 — Notice what money represents (solo — both partners)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Before the next financial conversation, one internal question:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When I think about money in this relationship, what do I feel — and where does it come from?"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For the one who monitors: is it concrete anxiety, or something older around instability, loss, the feeling of not being in control?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For the one who spends: is it a real need, a gesture of self-care, a territory of autonomy — or something looking to fill something else?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="No need to talk about it yet. Just name it, internally."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Level 2 — Separate money from power (solo — both partners)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A simple practice: the next time the financial question comes up, note mentally whether the conversation is about the numbers — or about something else. The budget, autonomy, trust, freedom, control."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If it's something else, the conversation about numbers will solve nothing. There's a different conversation to have — and it starts by naming what's really at stake."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Level 3 — Create space to talk about money differently (together)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A conversation about money can't happen in the moment the statement has just been checked. Not in the tension of the criticism, not in the defense that follows. It needs another space — chosen, calm, with a shared intention."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not a meeting. Not an audit. More like a moment decided together, outside any urgency, with one question as the entry point:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Can we talk about what money means to each of us — not about what was spent, but about what we want to build?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="That shift changes everything. We're no longer talking about numbers — we're talking about values, needs, what we imagine for the future. And from that place, things become possible that weren't possible in the kitchen, the bag still on the table."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few questions to structure this exchange:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;What does money represent for you in our relationship — concretely and symbolically?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;What have we never truly decided together — and that would deserve to be decided?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;What do you need to feel free — and what do I need to feel secure? Can we find something that serves both?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Can we set aside an envelope for each of us — money each person has freely, without having to justify it — and a shared envelope for joint decisions?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This isn't a win-lose negotiation. It's two people looking together for a system that respects both what one needs to feel grounded — and what the other needs to feel alive."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Level 4 — Name the game together (together)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few days after the scene, calmly:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I realize that when we talk about money, we're rarely just talking about money. I tend to monitor when I feel anxious — you tend to spend when you need space. Does that resonate?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not an accusation. A shared observation — that opens the possibility of talking about what's really happening."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="25471.5432569159" OwnPage="80" ItemID="225702864" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.519634868643" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="257684112" BACKITEM="225700032"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125984" YPOS="6413.28498919936" OwnPage="19" ItemID="239808912" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5290836875473" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle FONT="Algerian Regular" LANGUAGE="ee"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What We Really Need — the NVC Angle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When we're hurting in this scene, the natural reflex is to think the problem comes from the other person. That they don't do enough. That they don't understand. That they need to change."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This reflex is human. And it has a cost: as long as we wait for the other person to change before feeling better, we give them all the power over our state. We put ourselves in dependency."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="NVC (Nonviolent Communication) offers something different — and more demanding. It starts from the principle that my needs belong to me. They are not a consequence of what the other person does or doesn't do. And I am responsible for finding how to meet them."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="It's not "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="&quot;I need you to do your share"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; — that's a demand disguised as a need. It's &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I need efficiency — and here's how I choose to meet it."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The difference is enormous. In the first case, I'm waiting. In the second, I'm moving."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181102" YPOS="6413.28498919936" OwnPage="20" ItemID="239811744" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5290836875473" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="193595648" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle FONT="Algerian Regular" LANGUAGE="ee"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exercise — Identifying Your Deep Need"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Read the following list. For each need, the question isn't &quot;is the other person preventing me from having it?&quot; but &quot;is this need alive in me — and how do I choose to meet it?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Check the two or three that truly resonate."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Once your needs are identified, complete this sentence for each:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need __. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is __.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few examples to get you started:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need efficiency. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is take charge of the tasks I do quickly and well — and let go of the ones that aren't a priority for me.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need intimacy. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is finish quickly what needs to be done tonight — so I have time and energy to be truly present with the other person.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;I need mental space. When I reconnect to this need, what I choose to do is write down the tasks somewhere so I'm no longer carrying them in my head.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What you often observe after this exercise: the frustration toward the other person diminishes. Not because the distribution problem has been solved — but because you've reclaimed something. You're no longer waiting. You're moving."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="562.089125496481" YPOS="6504.97636959097" OwnPage="20" ItemID="239803248" PTYPE="2" WIDTH="334.95512229113" HEIGHT="233.295185004529" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="0.39" LOCALSCY="0.39" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" Pagenumber="0" PFILE="images/en/needchap1.png" PRFILE="Embedded sRGB built-in" IRENDER="0" EPROF="Embedded sRGB built-in" path="M0 0 L334.955 0 L334.955 233.295 L0 233.295 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L334.955 0 L334.955 233.295 L0 233.295 L0 0 Z" gXpos="562.089125496481" gYpos="6504.97636959097" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125985" YPOS="10860.2119183332" OwnPage="33" ItemID="239806080" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5268789631399" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="193561632" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Before the Analysis — One Important Thing"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you recognize yourself in this scene, it's probably because you've lived it. Not exactly like this — the words change, the time changes. But that evening, that silence, that dinner where nobody really looks at each other — you know what that's like."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And if you're the one who waited, you also know what it's like to spend the evening managing, organizing, holding things together — and to see the other person come home without seeming to grasp what that represents. The frustration building. The criticism coming out — not always in the form you would have wanted."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What you feel is real. It's not a bad mood. It's not irrational."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="But this booklet will offer you something a little uncomfortable: to also look at what's happening on your side. Not to minimize what you're going through. Not to say you're wrong. But because it's the only place from which you can truly change something."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="We can't change the other person. We can change what we do — and observe how the evening reconfigures."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What's Really Happening"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The scene you just read is not an argument about work schedules. What's happening here has almost nothing to do with the meeting that went on forever."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="While she waited, something built up. She managed the evening, the children perhaps, dinner, the ordinary mental load of a weekday night. And alongside that, without really choosing it, an accumulation happened. Not clear thoughts — more something diffuse. Uncertainty about what time he'd be home. The feeling of carrying things alone. And something deeper looking for a form."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When the door opens, that something looks for a way out. And it comes out the way it knows."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;You just don't care, that's all.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="That's not really what she wanted to say. Put clearly, it would sound more like: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I needed you tonight, and once again I didn't know what time you'd be home."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; But that sentence is too vulnerable. So it arrives dressed as a criticism."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And the criticism calls for a defense. And the defense confirms what she feared."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="On his side, he comes home exhausted. He didn't choose to come home late. He had a bad day. And the first thing he finds when he walks in is an accusation. He also needs something tonight — to be welcomed, to be seen, to breathe. But those needs won't be spoken either."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both are right about what they're experiencing. Neither is saying what they're really experiencing."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Game Being Played — Without Anyone Having Decided It"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There are three roles in this game. The "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the one who suffers, who waits, who carries. The "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the one who accuses, who criticizes. And the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Rescuer"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the one who patches things up, who smooths things over, who acts as if."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What's particularly tricky about this scene is that the game begins "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="before the door even opens"/>
                <ITEXT CH="."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="While waiting, she gradually slides into the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" position — alone, uncertain, carrying what could have been shared. This slide is not conscious. It's the situation that leads her there."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When he comes home, she shifts into "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — the criticism comes out, the accusation arrives. He enters as "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — he's on the receiving end, he justifies himself, he didn't choose to come home late."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Then the twist. &quot;You want to argue?&quot; — he shifts to "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=", and she becomes the "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" of the conflict she herself triggered. The silent dinner is the logical conclusion: both have lost, both have confirmed what they feared."/>
                <para PARENT="DIALOGUE"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What's revealing: she was in "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" mode before he said a word. The rumination during the wait was already the beginning of the game. Before he came home. Before he spoke."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" waiting → "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" on arrival → Defensive "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Victim"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" → "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="Persecutor"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" closing off → silence → both confirm what they feared"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="What Each Person Gets from It — the Hard Part"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This system persists because it confirms something for each person."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For her: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="he puts work before us."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; Every late return, every justification, every silent dinner feeds this conviction. And this conviction justifies the next criticism."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="For him: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="whatever I do, it's never enough."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; Every criticism, even when he's exhausted and acting in good faith, confirms that coming home is a minefield. And this conviction justifies the withdrawal — which will fuel the next criticism."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Both avoid the same thing — a real conversation about what each needs. And this avoidance slowly digs the distance that neither wants."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125985" YPOS="10224.9366427427" OwnPage="31" ItemID="239800416" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.527193923769" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="10224.9366427427" OwnPage="32" ItemID="239823072" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.527193923769" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Scene"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Apartment entrance, 8:30 pm. He comes in, visibly tired. She's in the kitchen, back turned."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;Evening. Sorry, meeting that went on forever.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Silence. She continues what she was doing."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;You just don't care, that's all.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;What? I had a terrible day.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Her: &quot;So did I.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="He puts his things down, exhales."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Him: &quot;You want to argue, is that it?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="She doesn't answer. Dinner passes without them really looking at each other."/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Do You Recognize Yourself?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="I experience this scene: never · sometimes · often"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="In this scene, I'm more like: the one coming home · the one who waited · both depending on the moment"/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="9589.66136715211" OwnPage="30" ItemID="239825904" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5275088843981" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Scene 2 — The Late Return"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <para PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Tell Me I Matter&quot;"/>
                <trail PARENT="Titre" ALIGN="1"/>
            </StoryText>
            <PageItemAttributes>
                <ItemAttribute Name="tdm" Type="string" Value="Scène 2 — Le retour tardif" Parameter="" Relationship="none" RelationshipTo="" AutoAddTo="none"/>
            </PageItemAttributes>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125985" YPOS="9589.66136715211" OwnPage="29" ItemID="239820240" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5275088843981" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125985" YPOS="8954.38609156156" OwnPage="27" ItemID="239814576" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5278238450272" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="239817408" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="One question per evening — not all at once, just the one for that day:"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Monday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Today, in this scene, was I more in the mode of rescuing, accusing, or suffering?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Tuesday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What did I avoid feeling by taking over — or by giving up?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Wednesday: What need was activated today — and how did I choose to meet it?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Thursday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What would have happened if I'd done things differently — just once?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Friday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="How did I nourish my Free Child today — and what did it change, even slightly?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Saturday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What am I confirming about the other person by repeating this system — and is that really true?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Sunday: "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What do I want to keep from this week — and what do I want to see differently next week?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If You Want to Explore This Together"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="To do calmly — not after an argument, not exhausted at the end of the evening. A moment when you're both available. Twenty minutes."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Part 1 — What Each Person Is Really Living (10 minutes)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Each person takes a sheet and completes these sentences alone, without showing the other:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;In the way we manage our home, what truly exhausts me is...&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;The need I'm trying to meet when I handle things the way I do is...&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;What I find hard to say about this is...&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Then you share. Each person reads what they wrote. The other listens — without interrupting, without defending, without explaining. Just hear."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This is not a debate. It's two people showing each other something true."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Part 2 — An Agreement That Respects Both (10 minutes)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="One question to explore together:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;How do we organize ourselves in a way that nourishes what matters to each of us — and leaves us both energy for something other than tasks?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not a chore list. A living agreement — that can be adjusted, revised, tested. With one rule: what's delegated belongs to the person doing it. Their way. Not the other's."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The next scene takes place at the apartment entrance. It's 8:30 pm. She hasn't said anything yet — and yet something has already begun."/>
                <trail PARENT="scene_page_subtitle" ALIGN="1"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="8954.38609156156" OwnPage="28" ItemID="239817408" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5278238450272" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="239814576"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125985" YPOS="8319.11081597101" OwnPage="25" ItemID="239834400" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5281388056563" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Feeding Your Free Child — A Practice in Its Own Right"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="There is something this booklet will repeat in every scene — because it's one of the simplest and least used keys."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="When we're exhausted, when we're carrying too much, when we're controlling because we feel that if we let go everything falls apart — it's often a sign that we've forgotten to nourish ourselves."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="In psychology, we talk about the Free Child — that part of you that plays, creates, feels, has fun without ulterior motives. The part that existed before you learned to be useful, responsible, reasonable. It hasn't disappeared. It's just waiting for a little space."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And here's what's interesting: when the Free Child is nourished, the need to control diminishes naturally. Not because you've decided to let go — but because you need to hold on less. You're less tense, less watchful, less inclined to redo. You have more energy to be truly present — for yourself and for the other person."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Some examples of what nourishes the Free Child:"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Doing something creative without a goal — drawing, cooking for pleasure, gardening, tinkering. Moving for the pleasure of it — dancing, walking without a destination, swimming. Learning something just because it's interesting — not useful, not productive, just curious. Playing — a game, an instrument, a sport, anything that has no goal other than the pleasure of playing. Resting truly — not recovering to produce better afterward. Resting because you feel like it. Doing something spontaneous — without planning, without optimizing, just because the urge is there."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="8319.11081597101" OwnPage="26" ItemID="239840064" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5281388056563" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="Free Child Tracker — 7 days"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Every evening, one minute. Not a review — just note."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The end-of-week"/>
                <ITEXT CPARENT="Default Character Style" CH=" "/>
                <ITEXT CH="question:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="On the days when I nourished my Free Child — did I have more or less urge to control, redo, carry? Is there a connection?"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Daily Tracking — 7 Days"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Every evening, two minutes."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="7683.83554038046" OwnPage="24" ItemID="239828736" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5284537662872" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="239837232"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="141.102992125985" YPOS="7683.83554038046" OwnPage="23" ItemID="239837232" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5284537662872" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="239828736" BACKITEM="239831568"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="560.630551181103" YPOS="7048.56026478991" OwnPage="22" ItemID="239831568" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="337.322834645669" HEIGHT="513.070866141732" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.323 0 L337.323 513.071 L0 513.071 L0 0 Z" gXpos="560.630551181103" gYpos="60.5287687269172" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="239837232" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <ITEXT CH="The Exits"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 1 — Notice your role in the moment"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The next time this scene is triggered, one internal question — quick, without analysis:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Right now, am I more in the mode of rescuing, accusing, or suffering?"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="No need for an elaborate answer. Just name it. This recognition creates a space — even a tiny one — between what's happening and what you do."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="rescuing"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — taking over before the other person has finished, redoing what was done — pause. One question:"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH=" is this truly necessary, or is it simply not the way I would have done it?"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" If it's the second reason: let it go. This time."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you're "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Bold" CH="suffering"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" — not trying, waiting for the other to take over — pause too. "/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="Do I really not know how — or have I learned that trying was pointless?"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" If it's the second reason: one attempt. Imperfect. But one attempt."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 2 — The Letting Go Experience (solo exercise)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This exercise is for the one who takes over. It requires a little courage."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This week, choose one task — just one — that you truly delegate. Not by explaining how to do it. Not by checking afterward. Just: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="can you take care of this this week?"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; And let go."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="It doesn't matter if it's done differently. It doesn't matter if it's not exactly as you would have done it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And note three things:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What was done is..."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; — name what was accomplished. Truly accomplished. Not what's missing."/>
                <para PARENT="DIALOGUE"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What this freed up for me was..."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot; — what were you able to do, or not do, during that time? Rest? A moment for yourself? Just breathe?"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="What I wanted to correct but let go was.."/>
                <ITEXT CH=".&quot; — note the resistance. Without acting on it. Just observe it."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The goal is not to accept disorder forever. It's to see, just once, what control costs — and what letting go gives."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 3 — Reconnect to your need (solo)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="The next time frustration builds in this scene, before saying anything — an internal pause."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Go back to your list of identified needs above. And complete mentally:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;Right now, the need that's activated in me is __. And what I choose to do to meet it is __.&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="This shift — even done silently, even in thirty seconds — changes something. You move from reaction to choice."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 4 — Move from criticism to need (together)"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="If you want to talk to the other person — and only if the moment is calm, not right after a tension — a different way to open the conversation."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Instead of: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="you never do anything, it's always me doing everything."/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Try: &quot;"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Times New Roman Italic" CH="I realized something. What exhausts me most isn't the tasks themselves — it's having them all in my head constantly. Can we figure out together how to lighten that"/>
                <ITEXT CH="?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="It's not the same conversation. The first is an accusation — it calls for a defense. The second is an invitation — it can call for a response."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Exit 5 — Build something together (together)"/>
                <para PARENT="scene_page_subtitle"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A conversation to have calmly, an evening when you're not exhausted. Twenty minutes."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Not to decide who does what on a chart. To understand what really matters to each of you — and build something from there."/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A few questions to get started:"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;In our home, what truly matters to you — and what matters less?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;What do you prefer doing — and what do you find truly unpleasant?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="&quot;How can we organize ourselves in a way that respects what matters to each of us?&quot;"/>
                <para PARENT="narration"/>
                <para PARENT="BODY"/>
                <ITEXT CH="And an implicit rule to set together, if possible: what's delegated belongs to the person doing it. Their way. Not yours. The result is what matters — not the path to get there."/>
                <trail PARENT="BODY"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
